@@ -816,8 +816,29 @@ label values are equal, elements are sorted by their full label sets.
 Please note that `sort_by_label` only affects the results of instant queries, as
 range query results always have a fixed output ordering.

-`sort_by_label` uses [natural sort
-order](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_sort_order).
+`sort_by_label` compares label values by their type, so that a label whose
+values mix different representations still has a stable total order. Each label
+value is parsed into the most specific type it can be read as, values of
+different types are ordered by their type, and values of the same type are
+ordered by their parsed value:
+
+| Type | Examples | Ordered by |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| leading whitespace | `" 1"`, `"\tfoo"` | Values with leading whitespace are never typed and sort before all other values. |
+| positive infinity | `+Inf`, `Infinity` | – |
+| number | `1`, `-2.5`, `+1.5e-3` | Numeric value. A bare exponent marker like `1e` is not a number, and neither is `NaN`. |
+| negative infinity | `-Inf` | – |
+| duration | `500ms`, `-1.5h`, `1h30m`, `1e3s` | Length, with `ns`, `us`, `ms`, `s`, `m`, `h`, `d`, `w` and `y` as units. |
+| byte size | `512B`, `1kB`, `1.5GiB`, `1e3MB` | Number of bytes, with decimal (`kB`) and binary (`KiB`) units. |
+| semantic version | `1.2.3`, `v2.0.0-rc.1` | [Semantic versioning](https://semver.org/) precedence, with an optional leading `v`. Anything that is not a valid semantic version is not a version. |
+| IP address | `10.0.0.1`, `2001:db8::1` | Address, IPv4 before IPv6. IPv4-mapped IPv6 addresses count as IPv6. |
+| CIDR prefix | `10.0.0.0/8`, `2001:db8::/32` | Network address, IPv4 before IPv6, less specific prefixes first. |
+| timestamp | `2024-01-02`, `2024-01-02T15:04:05Z` | Point in time. |
+| anything else | `canary`, `4m1000`, `""` | [Natural sort order](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_sort_order). |
+
+Numbers, durations and byte sizes keep their order for arbitrarily large
+magnitudes. Values that are equal after parsing are ordered by natural sort
+order of the original label values.

 ## `sort_by_label_desc()`

